    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d473">

                <pb facs="0831" n="735" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg735"/>

                <head>No. 471.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Foster to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1874-03-12"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 12, 1874</date>.
                        (Received March 26.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 121.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Pursuant to the indication contained in
                    your No. 71, of the 29th of January last, I addressed a note to the minister of
                    foreign affairs on the 28th ultimo, (inclosure 1,) informing him that the
                    promised statement of Mexican bonds sold in the United States would be awaited
                    with interest by my Government; and on the 10th instant I received, in reply
                    thereto; the brief memorandum (inclosure 2) which I inclose.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JOHN W. FOSTER.</signed></closer>




                <xi:include href="d473-a1.xml" xpointer="d473-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d473-a2.xml" xpointer="d473-a2"/>
